'''# MedSync Health, Inc.
# Data Processing Agreement (DPA)

**Version:** 2.0
**Effective Date:** January 1, 2026

This Data Processing Agreement ("DPA") is entered into between MedSync Health, Inc. ("Processor") and the customer ("Controller") and is incorporated into the Master Subscription Agreement.

## 1. Definitions

- **"Controller"** means the entity which determines the purposes and means of the Processing of Personal Data.
- **"Processor"** means MedSync Health, Inc.
- **"Personal Data"** means any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person.
- **"Protected Health Information" (PHI)** has the meaning set forth under the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act of 1996 (HIPAA).

## 2. Processing of Personal Data

- **Processor's Role:** The Processor will process Personal Data, including PHI, on behalf of the Controller for the sole purpose of providing the MedSync Platform services.
- **Compliance with Laws:** The Processor will comply with all applicable data protection laws, including GDPR and HIPAA.

## 3. Data Security

- **Security Measures:** The Processor will implement and maintain appropriate technical and organizational security measures to protect Personal Data against unauthorized or unlawful processing and against accidental loss, destruction, damage, alteration, or disclosure. These measures are detailed in our Security & Compliance documentation.

## 4. Sub-processors

- The Processor may engage third-party sub-processors to process Personal Data on its behalf. A list of current sub-processors is available upon request.

## 5. Data Subject Rights

- The Processor will assist the Controller in responding to data subject requests to exercise their rights under applicable data protection laws.

## 6. Data Breach Notification

- In the event of a data breach, the Processor will notify the Controller without undue delay after becoming aware of the breach.

## 7. Data Transfers

- The Processor will not transfer Personal Data outside of the European Economic Area (EEA) or the United States without ensuring appropriate safeguards are in place.

## 8. Audits

- The Processor will make available to the Controller all information necessary to demonstrate compliance with this DPA and will allow for and contribute to audits, including inspections, conducted by the Controller or another auditor mandated by the Controller.
